export const HOW_HTML = "<div class=\"eyebrow\">isaac-perez-co · static · Vercel</div><h1 class=\"t\">How it's built</h1><div class=\"sub\">A playable room at /, readable personal page at /about/, six retained utility pages</div>\n<h3 class=\"sec\">The two personal routes</h3>\n<p><b>The room is the homepage.</b> It is a first-person, toy-eye-level visit to Isaac's approved bedroom and connected bathroom. Visitors can meet Mimi and Charlie, inspect shoes and collectibles, interact with the desk, change music and lighting, and optionally capture three live photos for a downloadable postcard. The room uses a 70-inch desk and queen mattress as scale anchors; enclosed and hidden details inferred from photos are approximate.</p>\n<p><code>/about/</code> preserves the prior Me → Experience → My company editorial page, with the original portrait and quiet personal contact footer. Its existing copy, work history, education, company section and links are the source for in-room stories and the desk monitor. It is a direct reading alternative that does not require WebGL.</p>\n<h3 class=\"sec\">Runtime and asset boundary</h3>\n<pre>IsaacPerez.co/\n  index.html             playable room at /\n  room/                  public JS, CSS, room and cat GLBs, short film\n  about/index.html       preserved editorial page and /about/# anchors\n  css/personal.css       editorial page styling\n  js/personal.js         editorial theme and reveal behavior\n  photo/pricing/         retained pricing page\n  shootsort/             retained macOS download page\n  roommate/              three Quarters app pages\n  souvenir/privacy/      Souvenir app privacy page\n  docs/room-preview/     source, prototype and provenance; not deployed</pre>\n<p>The root loads a small same-origin WebGL viewer and curated room assets from <code>/room/</code>. The editable scene, local reference-photo panel and original multi-angle photographs stay in <code>docs/room-preview/</code> or Isaac's Downloads and are withheld by <code>.vercelignore</code>. A self-hosted five-second Seedance 2.5 material study is optional cinema, not the playable scene. The room's lo-fi/house music and toy cues are made locally with Web Audio; no streaming service, external player, framework, build step, account or backend is involved.</p>\n<p><code>/room/portfolio.js</code> fetches <code>/about/</code> on first use so the game does not fork the biography. <code>/room/photo-safari.js</code> captures the live canvas and composes a postcard in page memory; visitor images are not uploaded. /about/ retains its inline pre-paint theme script, existing storage preference and reduced-motion-aware scroll behavior. Existing utility-page scripts remain separate.</p>\n<h3 class=\"sec\">Public routes</h3>\n<pre>/                       room homepage\n/about/                 preserved editorial page\n/photo/pricing/         retained pricing\n/shootsort/             retained download page\n/souvenir/privacy/      app privacy\n/roommate/privacy/      Quarters privacy\n/roommate/terms/        Quarters terms\n/roommate/support/      Quarters support</pre>\n<p>All eight are in <code>sitemap.xml</code> with exact canonicals. Utility-page section links target <code>/about/#about</code>, <code>/about/#experience</code>, <code>/about/#firstunit</code> and <code>/about/#contact</code>; Home returns to the room. <code>/photo</code> and <code>/photo/</code> remain HTTP 308 redirects to <code>https://firstunit.io/fu-0001</code>. The legal pages and their paths remain unchanged.</p>\n<h3 class=\"sec\">Hosting and review</h3>\n<p>Vercel serves this repository directly from <code>main</code>. <code>vercel.json</code> owns security headers and photo redirects; <code>.vercelignore</code> excludes repository-only documents and the local room source. Exact filename case, asset references, sitemap paths, CSP hashes and pricing copy are checked with <code>tools/check-site.sh</code>. Fleet hooks enforce Conventional Commits. A push to main is production publication, so review the root room, /about/ and retained routes in a local or preview deployment first.</p>\n<p>Edit this architecture through <code>docs/atlas/data.mjs</code> and rebuild both generated views.</p>";
